<title>UK: SAVE &amp; PROSPER PLANS E.EUROPE INVESTMENT VEHICLE.</title>
<headline>SAVE &amp; PROSPER PLANS E.EUROPE INVESTMENT VEHICLE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK investment house Save &amp; Prosper said on Wednesday it would launch an open ended investment company, to be managed by its owner Flemings.</p>
<p>An East European fund would form the first &quot;spoke&quot; of the new company, Save &amp; Prosper said in a statement.</p>
<p>Details of the fund will be announced next month, but it will be investing in Russia, Poland and Hungary amongst other markets.</p>
<p>It will be run by Stefan Bottcher, who already runs the Fleming Flagship East European Fund, now valued at $570 million.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6414</p>
